<title>USA: US banks seek big changes to financial reform bill.</title>
<headline>US banks seek big changes to financial reform bill.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The American Bankers Association on Monday said it would oppose legislation to overhaul U.S. financial laws unless &quot;major changes&quot; are made in the proposal.</p>
<p>The legislation, now before the Commerce Committee in the House of Representatives, would eliminate the legal barriers contained in the 1933 Glass Steagall Act that separate banking from other financial service industries. &quot;There is a strong consensus throughout the banking industry that this bill needs reconstructive surgery, not just cosmetic changes,&quot; Walter Dods, the association's president, said.</p>
</text>
